# Over-general names -- questions that SHOULD be ambiguous, and are labelled as such.
#
# The export publishes the same detail name under several indicators: seven details are
# called "Sector Exports", eight "Sector Contribution To GDP", two "Global Cybersecurity
# Index (GCI) Rank", and "Japan", "Others" and "India" each name a column of three
# different export breakdowns. A reader typing one of these has genuinely not said which
# they mean.
#
# They are in the set because they are AD-30's structural lesson in miniature: every
# member of the expected set scores *identically*, so no floor and no ranking can separate
# them. Counting them as hits when any member comes back is the honest measurement; a set
# that labelled one arbitrary member as the answer would report a 1-in-8 accident as a
# retrieval failure and make the floor look worse than it is.

[ambig-en-001]
lang: en
kind: ambiguous
question: Sector Exports
expect: 122d47f7-8c5c-48a5-fd90-08dddd5433de, d1cc2d84-2557-4443-ce7b-08de268d1812, 99d78879-ebc5-44fc-6d8d-08de8e443779, 902de7d7-c5ac-444a-7ab1-08dec461c23d, 6306cb7f-91a1-456e-8716-08dee641c19a, ba5871a1-f81c-43c3-c7bd-08de3ade590a, eb07919f-adb5-4e98-7ab0-08dec461c23d
why: Seven details publish this name or a name beginning with it, under seven sectors.

[ambig-en-002]
lang: en
kind: ambiguous
question: Sector Contribution To GDP
expect: c4a4da88-830d-4098-87d8-08dea2214fb6, a08d961b-cfd0-4fcf-aead-08deb3df601c, 70e23b54-5476-492a-7a4a-08dec461c23d, d14eadeb-a8bf-4242-92c8-08dec462e127, 89f1fdc0-cf06-4569-d2e8-08ded4dc1597, 1d19eeb1-9bc7-4998-a7a4-08def0866aac, f60a0ecf-94f5-4f69-a7aa-08def0866aac, cf835ee5-5215-4fdf-6f92-08dea8e8edb6
why: Eight sectors publish a detail of exactly this name; only the English *label* carries the sector, and in two of the eight only the Arabic one does.

